    "K_t": "Evidence:\n[1] With \"Fast\" also reaching number one in April 2017, Bryan became the first artist in the chart's history to achieve six number one singles from one album.\n[2] The group was also popular in Canada, having three number-one singles in the country.\n[3] His singles since 2008 have all been released to the country music format, where he has seven number-one singles: \"Don't Think I Don't Think About It\", \"It Won't Be Like This for Long\", \"Alright\", \"Come Back Song\", \"This\", \"Wagon Wheel\", and \"If I Told You\".\n[4] As a solo artist, his discography comprises five studio albums, including four for Capitol Nashville."
